/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-45-    Rule:\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-46-    - Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-47-    - On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-48-    - Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-49-    - If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-50-\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-51-    Key insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-52-    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-53-    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-54-    H, W = g.shape\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-55-\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-56-    template_bg = int(g[0, 0])\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-57-\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-58-    # Path is the most frequent color != template_bg.\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-59-    counts = Counter(map(int, g.flatten()))\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-60-    path_color = int(max([(cnt, int(col)) for col, cnt in counts.items() if int(col) != int(template_bg)])[1])\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-61-    _assert_path_single_component(g, path_color)\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-62-\\\\\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py-63-    # Detect the repeating cycle from 2x2 blocks in th